# What the `genlayer` job in .github/workflows/gates.yml asks for, before resolution.
#
# The job installs the COMPILED sibling, `ci-genlayer.txt`, which names this set plus everything it
# drags in, each with its hashes. This file is the intent; that one is what runs.
#
# THIS SET NEEDS PYTHON >= 3.12, UNLIKE ITS THREE SIBLINGS. `genlayer-py`, `genlayer-test` and
# `genvm-linter` all declare `requires_python: ">=3.12"` (or `>=3.10` for the linter, but its own
# runtime dependency on the other two forces 3.12 anyway) - this repository's own interpreter is
# 3.10 (GL-harness-notes.md, D-63). `pip-compile`, which compiled the other three `.in` files, runs
# under THIS repository's 3.10 and cannot resolve this set at all: it would refuse before touching
# the network, the same way installing it here would. Regenerate this one file differently, from a
# real Python 3.12 (the isolated `~/orchestra/glenv` this project already builds for T-GL-02):
#
#   uv pip compile --generate-hashes --python 3.12 --override /tmp/gl-override.txt \
#       -o requirements/ci-genlayer.txt requirements/ci-genlayer.in
#
# where /tmp/gl-override.txt contains one line, `genlayer-py==0.18.0` - NEEDED because
# `genlayer-test==0.29.2`'s own PUBLISHED PyPI metadata declares `genlayer-py<0.17.0,>=0.13.0`,
# which conflicts with the pin below (GL-harness-notes.md SS7a: checked against the actual source at
# the git tag that same release is built from, which declares `>=0.18.0,<0.19.0` - the PyPI
# metadata is stale, not the pin). `--override` forces the resolver to accept 0.18.0 anyway; the
# override file itself is not committed, because the flag is only needed to WALK the dependency
# graph during compilation - the resulting `ci-genlayer.txt` is a flat, fully pinned closure that
# does not re-resolve anything at install time.
#
# THE SAME STALE METADATA ALSO BREAKS A PLAIN `pip install` OF THE COMPILED FILE (measured: pip's
# resolver refuses the same conflict `uv` needed the override for). `requirements/ci-genlayer.txt`
# is therefore installed with `--no-deps` in both `gates.yml` and `scripts/push.sh` - safe here,
# unlike an ordinary use of that flag, because the compiled file already names the FULL correct
# transitive closure with hashes; `--no-deps` only tells pip not to recompute a graph it would get
# wrong from the same bad metadata.
genlayer-py==0.18.0
genlayer-test==0.29.2
genvm-linter==0.11.0
